WEBVTT

00:00.560 --> 00:01.840
O, my friend!

00:01.840 --> 00:04.440
This is a victory for us!

00:04.500 --> 00:07.600
Our fame starts here!

00:07.640 --> 00:08.600
O, my friend!

00:08.600 --> 00:13.900
Let us celebrate this victory
for the next battle!

00:28.540 --> 00:34.080
"I died for naught" I won't
let it end like that for you

00:34.080 --> 00:39.340
until I am the last one standing

00:39.340 --> 00:42.320
The enemy is cruel... We will kill

00:42.320 --> 00:45.360
The enemy is colossal... We will jump

00:45.360 --> 00:49.000
In our hands we hold blades of glory

00:49.000 --> 00:51.280
and sing in the name of victory

00:51.280 --> 00:55.920
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

00:57.240 --> 01:03.360
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

01:03.380 --> 01:07.900
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

01:09.480 --> 01:11.800
and soar through the sky

01:11.860 --> 01:16.060
with our wings of freedom

01:29.980 --> 01:34.990
Smile: Assault on Stohess, Part 1

01:37.540 --> 01:39.160
Keep it up, Annie!

01:41.980 --> 01:44.260
That's my daughter!

01:46.130 --> 01:48.580
What are you doing? Don't stop!

02:03.790 --> 02:05.740
Wall Sina
Eastern Wall City

02:05.740 --> 02:06.870
Huh? Didn't you hear?

02:06.870 --> 02:11.020
The Titan boy and his companions
were summoned by the King.

02:11.210 --> 02:13.410
They'll be passing through the city today.

02:13.410 --> 02:14.460
I see.

02:14.460 --> 02:17.530
He's gonna wind up getting
dissected for sure this time.

02:17.530 --> 02:23.530
Either way, I just hope things work
out so they'll seal the gates.

02:24.540 --> 02:28.220
What?! Did you just say "seal the gates"?

02:28.220 --> 02:32.080
Do you want to further defile our
gods with lowly human meddling?!

02:33.580 --> 02:37.090
Maria! Rose! Sina!

02:37.090 --> 02:41.980
How dare you even suggest desecrating
our three sacred goddesses?!

02:41.980 --> 02:44.720
He's one of those crazies who
worship the Walls as gods.

02:44.720 --> 02:45.630
Just ignore him.

02:45.630 --> 02:48.700
Indeed... Those freaks still exist...

02:48.700 --> 02:50.230
Damn it.
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

02:50.230 --> 02:55.000
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

02:55.000 --> 02:55.080
Stohess Military Police Branch
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

02:55.080 --> 02:58.390
Stohess Military Police Branch

03:00.910 --> 03:03.160
You're finally up.

03:03.160 --> 03:07.160
You looked so scary in your sleep
nobody dared to wake you up.

03:07.160 --> 03:09.400
Sorry, Annie.

03:09.400 --> 03:11.420
You've been slacking off a lot recently.

03:12.070 --> 03:15.800
What? Are you mad?

03:15.800 --> 03:17.670
How are we supposed to get along?

03:17.670 --> 03:22.280
Leave her be. She's from Trost, remember.

03:22.280 --> 03:25.190
She's the only person in this branch
with any actual combat experience.

03:25.190 --> 03:29.190
Of course she can't smile cheerfully
when she's just returned from hell.

03:29.430 --> 03:34.560
Oh, I get it. So you like her?

03:34.560 --> 03:36.460
I wonder what you see in her.

03:36.460 --> 03:42.040
Hitch... There's only one way a dimwitted
chick like you gets into the Military Police.

03:42.420 --> 03:45.740
What's that? I wouldn't know.

03:45.770 --> 03:46.660
Tell me?

03:46.660 --> 03:47.850
Shut up, you two.

03:52.830 --> 03:54.860
Don't bother.

03:55.570 --> 03:59.260
Today you'll be doing something
other than your usual chores.

03:59.260 --> 04:00.860
That's why I ordered you to assemble here.

04:01.380 --> 04:05.130
A unit from the Recon Corps has
been summoned by the King.

04:05.540 --> 04:09.370
They're passing through the
city's main street today.

04:10.030 --> 04:12.910
Escorting them to the capitol is
Military Police HQ's responsibility,

04:12.910 --> 04:15.880
so we only need to accompany
them as they pass through town.

04:16.430 --> 04:19.860
The use of 3D Maneuver Gear will be
temporarily permitted within city limits.

04:19.860 --> 04:23.390
You will guard the convoy in
tandem with their own security.

04:23.390 --> 04:28.260
You'll travel by barge to
the mission starting point.

04:28.780 --> 04:30.680
May I ask a question?

04:30.680 --> 04:32.420
What?

04:32.420 --> 04:35.650
What are we protecting the convoy from?

04:38.510 --> 04:42.860
I'm unaware of any people within
this Wall who'd oppose the King.

04:43.240 --> 04:45.480
Even if we've overlooked some petty criminals,

04:45.480 --> 04:48.490
truly organized opposition
would be unimaginable,

04:48.510 --> 04:51.310
unless they had a stronghold
outside the Wall.

04:51.310 --> 04:53.140
Why would anyone even try such
a thing in the first place?

04:53.140 --> 04:55.520
Oh, well aren't you clever?

04:55.520 --> 04:57.340
I'm putting you in charge.

04:57.340 --> 05:00.010
The details are all here.

05:03.180 --> 05:08.460
We officers are really busy. You
can handle this yourselves.

05:09.680 --> 05:12.190
Just don't screw it up.

05:12.890 --> 05:15.200
Sorry for the wait, guys. Where were we?

05:15.200 --> 05:16.780
Whose turn is it?

05:21.920 --> 05:23.950
Those damn bastards!

05:23.950 --> 05:29.180
Yeah... The Military Police are
even more rotten than I imagined.

05:29.180 --> 05:32.280
That's why I picked being an MP, but still...

05:32.280 --> 05:36.740
They force us rookies to handle everything.

05:36.740 --> 05:39.120
I didn't expect that.

05:39.120 --> 05:43.180
Scumbags. They can't think
of anything but themselves.

05:43.180 --> 05:44.220
Fucking scumbags.

05:44.960 --> 05:47.220
What are you talking about, Marlo?

05:47.220 --> 05:50.600
You joined the Police too. You're no better.

05:52.740 --> 05:56.150
I'm not the same. I'm not scum like you guys.

05:56.900 --> 06:00.360
I came here to correct the Military Police!

06:02.840 --> 06:07.070
Impressive, Marlo! So that's how you roll?

06:07.070 --> 06:08.910
And how will you fix things?

06:09.310 --> 06:11.870
I'll have to work my way to the top.

06:11.870 --> 06:18.200
When I'm in charge, I will enforce
the rules and punish corruption.

06:18.200 --> 06:19.250
It's that simple.

06:20.300 --> 06:23.420
I'll make the Police a place
for normal people again.

06:23.420 --> 06:24.300
That's all.

06:24.950 --> 06:27.370
The way humans are meant to be!

06:29.120 --> 06:32.170
Holy shit, you're the real deal!

06:32.170 --> 06:35.560
Here I thought you were a total bore!
So sorry!

06:36.340 --> 06:40.880
What a noble goal you have. Do your best.

06:40.880 --> 06:42.040
I wonder.

06:43.030 --> 06:46.640
If a "good person" like you
controlled the system,

06:46.640 --> 06:48.820
that'd be the end for us, I think.

06:48.820 --> 06:52.080
What? You can actually speak?

06:52.850 --> 06:55.620
I think you're right.

06:56.010 --> 06:57.760
You say all the correct things.

06:58.400 --> 07:00.840
I know another person much like you.

07:01.890 --> 07:06.680
You need a lot of courage to
go against the greater flow.

07:06.680 --> 07:08.080
I can respect that.

07:09.050 --> 07:12.080
But that doesn't mean you're not an idiot.

07:12.870 --> 07:15.560
Maybe it's just that the other
person you know is an idiot.

07:15.740 --> 07:17.310
I'm different from him!

07:19.410 --> 07:21.180
We've wasted too much time talking.

07:21.180 --> 07:22.220
Let's move out!

07:28.240 --> 07:31.870
The convoy will pass through
the outer gate in 45 minutes.

07:31.870 --> 07:35.910
Once we're there, everyone confirm
your designated positions.

07:35.910 --> 07:36.720
Got it?

07:36.720 --> 07:38.330
Yeah, yeah.

07:42.820 --> 07:44.380
Hey!

07:45.660 --> 07:46.880
What's going on?

07:47.250 --> 07:49.090
Aren't those ours?

07:49.290 --> 07:50.940
They must be taking them
to the Inner District.

07:50.940 --> 07:54.350
Even so, having the merchants
involved is unusual.

07:55.460 --> 07:57.540
What are they up to?

08:05.280 --> 08:08.280
They're selling our emergency backups?!

08:10.520 --> 08:12.810
Wait, what about the mission?

08:12.810 --> 08:16.030
Holy shit, he really is the real deal!

08:16.030 --> 08:18.760
Guess we'll see if that's
for better or for worse...

08:18.760 --> 08:20.540
For now let's just enjoy the show.

08:28.190 --> 08:30.620
Let's grab a drink then.

08:33.460 --> 08:36.360
What is it, rookie? What do you want?

08:36.360 --> 08:40.890
E-Embezzling emergency
backup supplies is a crime!

08:41.780 --> 08:42.690
So?

08:44.460 --> 08:49.900
Emergency goods are paid for by
the people's tax dollars and...

08:51.660 --> 08:55.530
So you think you can lecture
your superiors, rookie?

08:55.800 --> 08:59.120
I look forward to your future.

09:01.330 --> 09:04.310
For now, go buy yourself a
hooker and chill the fuck out.

09:06.360 --> 09:08.240
H-Hold it!

09:09.000 --> 09:11.010
Embezzling is...

09:34.090 --> 09:35.120
Hey!

09:38.600 --> 09:41.540
I'll have you arrested for
insubordination and treason.

09:42.110 --> 09:44.630
Damn you! You can't get away...

09:44.630 --> 09:45.920
Yes, we can.

09:46.790 --> 09:48.210
Here, we can!

09:51.010 --> 09:53.550
I think that's probably enough.

09:56.040 --> 10:00.560
Sorry if this retard was causing you trouble.

10:01.140 --> 10:04.580
We'll be sure he learns his lesson.

10:04.580 --> 10:06.150
Unless...

10:07.030 --> 10:10.980
You'd prefer to make a bigger scene?

10:14.060 --> 10:15.980
We'll let you off this once.

10:15.980 --> 10:16.880
Yes, sir!

10:20.100 --> 10:22.320
Let's go grab that drink now.

10:22.320 --> 10:24.750
Why not do it?

10:36.370 --> 10:43.980
Weren't you going to punish corruption?

10:44.840 --> 10:48.260
If you want, I'll help out.

10:53.900 --> 10:54.860
What did you wanna get?

10:54.860 --> 10:55.900
What else?

10:56.080 --> 10:57.210
Meat!

11:00.990 --> 11:01.990
Damn it!

11:04.050 --> 11:07.880
We know you're working really hard!

11:07.880 --> 11:10.540
Oh, I'm not worthy of your praise.

11:13.440 --> 11:15.470
That guy you know...

11:16.700 --> 11:19.170
That idiot you mentioned earlier...

11:19.170 --> 11:20.300
Would he have done it?

11:23.520 --> 11:24.720
Maybe.

11:29.320 --> 11:36.720
Then I'm just another piece of trash, caught
up in that greater flow you mentioned earlier.

11:36.720 --> 11:38.100
Am I not?

11:38.960 --> 11:40.740
Who knows?

11:42.280 --> 11:46.250
But isn't that what normal human beings do?

11:47.840 --> 11:56.480
I don't care if I'm swept along by the flow,
as long as I'm still considered a human.

12:20.520 --> 12:21.480
Annie!

12:33.920 --> 12:34.880
Hey.

12:35.260 --> 12:38.380
You're fitting in well
with the Military Police.

12:40.260 --> 12:41.480
Armin...

12:54.520 --> 12:57.190
What's with that look?

12:57.190 --> 12:59.470
I disguised myself as a porter.

12:59.470 --> 13:03.370
The cloak can hide my 3D Maneuver Gear.

13:03.970 --> 13:05.000
See?

13:06.060 --> 13:07.700
What's going on?

13:08.480 --> 13:13.170
Annie, would you assist
me in letting Eren escape?

13:13.340 --> 13:15.300
Escape to where?

13:15.300 --> 13:19.740
Where could you go inside these
Walls after disobeying the King?

13:19.740 --> 13:22.320
We'd just hide out for a while.

13:22.320 --> 13:25.090
We don't intend to go
against the King head-on.

13:25.390 --> 13:29.500
It'll be reported as a rebellion
by a portion of the Recon Corps.

13:29.500 --> 13:30.990
We need to buy time.

13:31.010 --> 13:35.450
Time to collect proof that could change
the outcome of the court martial.

13:35.450 --> 13:36.730
We will succeed.

13:37.270 --> 13:39.840
Change the outcome?

13:39.840 --> 13:42.250
Does anything so convenient even exist?

13:42.610 --> 13:43.570
What's your evidence?

13:46.140 --> 13:48.120
Sorry, but I can't say.

13:51.040 --> 13:54.040
I'm sorry too, but I can't help you like this.

13:54.220 --> 13:57.320
Good luck with whatever you're doing.

13:58.470 --> 14:01.060
Annie! Please!

14:01.060 --> 14:02.800
They're gonna wind up executing Eren!

14:04.800 --> 14:10.040
Clueless people will push mankind
down the path of extinction

14:10.040 --> 14:13.160
just for personal gain,
without even realizing it!

14:13.160 --> 14:15.880
I know my reasoning isn't all that convincing.

14:16.310 --> 14:17.820
But even so...

14:17.820 --> 14:20.560
Gambling big is our only chance at this point!

14:21.820 --> 14:25.760
Of course, we'll do our utmost to
avoid causing trouble for you.

14:25.760 --> 14:29.680
But to get through the
security inside Wall Sina,

14:29.680 --> 14:32.330
we need insider help from the Military Police.

14:33.590 --> 14:34.980
We have no other choice.

14:36.510 --> 14:41.340
Do I look like such a good person to you?

14:42.070 --> 14:43.600
"Good person"?

14:43.600 --> 14:49.350
Well... I don't like that term.

14:49.520 --> 14:56.500
To me, it seems like the meaning of "good
person" is really a person who's good for you.

14:57.100 --> 15:01.610
In that sense, I don't think any individual
can be "good" in everyone's eyes.

15:01.610 --> 15:05.750
So if you don't help us...

15:07.110 --> 15:10.620
Then, in my eyes, you'd be a bad person.

15:28.160 --> 15:29.140
Very well.

15:35.730 --> 15:37.050
I'm in.

15:48.850 --> 15:52.330
We made it through more
easily than I expected.

15:52.330 --> 15:56.860
That's the Military Police for you.
You can tell how hard they work.

15:56.860 --> 15:58.330
Stop glancing around so much.

15:58.740 --> 16:02.060
Let's just hope they don't
discover Jean's taken my place.

16:02.060 --> 16:04.300
I doubt that cover will last long.

16:04.920 --> 16:08.170
We look nothing alike.

16:08.390 --> 16:10.070
Don't worry.

16:10.070 --> 16:13.930
You both share a villainous face and
a sociopathic look in your eyes.

16:14.150 --> 16:16.330
I don't have a horseface like him!

16:16.330 --> 16:21.810
Hey, if I didn't agree to help, how
were you planning to get over the Wall?

16:22.180 --> 16:25.070
I was going to use the 3D
Maneuver Gear to break through.

16:25.240 --> 16:26.840
That's insane.

16:26.840 --> 16:32.820
Wouldn't it have been less troublesome
to escape before you reached Stohess?

16:33.190 --> 16:35.840
Why here? Why now?

16:35.840 --> 16:38.020
I thought the dense layout of the urban area

16:38.020 --> 16:41.830
would give us a better shot
at swapping Jean for Eren.

16:41.830 --> 16:47.010
Plus, pretending to follow
obediently instead of opposing them

16:47.040 --> 16:50.330
outright will buy us
more time to flee.

16:51.560 --> 16:54.750
I see. That makes sense.

16:59.250 --> 17:00.460
There!

17:09.400 --> 17:10.730
Here?

17:10.730 --> 17:13.050
Yeah. We'll go through here.

17:13.490 --> 17:17.640
It's the abandoned remains of an
underground city they planned long ago.

17:19.880 --> 17:23.870
This leads as far as the outer gate.

17:23.870 --> 17:26.040
Really? That's great!

17:27.640 --> 17:28.750
Annie?

17:29.260 --> 17:34.390
What's wrong? Don't tell me you're
scared of cramped, dark places?

17:35.360 --> 17:37.930
In fact, I am afraid.

17:38.520 --> 17:42.570
I doubt a brave, borderline-suicidal
guy like you could possibly

17:42.600 --> 17:45.720
understand the feelings
of a weak maiden like me.

17:49.110 --> 17:54.240
Someone who can fling a man head over heels in
mid-air with ease can't call herself a maiden.

17:54.240 --> 17:56.200
Stop being silly and hurry up!

17:56.200 --> 17:58.450
No, I'm not going that way.

17:59.870 --> 18:01.930
It scares me.

18:01.930 --> 18:04.870
If we don't travel above ground, I won't help.

18:15.300 --> 18:16.840
What are you even saying?!

18:16.840 --> 18:19.560
Get down here already! Stop screwing around!

18:19.560 --> 18:20.960
Eren, don't shout.

18:20.960 --> 18:23.090
It shouldn't be an issue, right, Mikasa?

18:24.310 --> 18:30.820
For some reason, there haven't been
any people nearby for a while now.

18:38.640 --> 18:41.660
Jeez! I'm hurt.

18:44.370 --> 18:51.610
When did you start looking at
me with those eyes, Armin?

18:53.040 --> 18:55.220
Annie, why?

18:56.120 --> 18:59.300
Why did you have Marco's 3D Maneuver Gear?

19:04.080 --> 19:06.860
I recognized even its tiniest marks and dings

19:06.860 --> 19:09.190
because we repaired ours together.

19:09.990 --> 19:11.980
That's how I knew.

19:12.360 --> 19:13.370
I see...

19:14.440 --> 19:17.610
Well, I happened to pick it up.

19:19.740 --> 19:25.380
Then you killed those two
Titans we captured alive?

19:25.380 --> 19:26.810
Who knows?

19:27.450 --> 19:32.530
But if you thought so a month
ago, why didn't you act?

19:32.530 --> 19:35.210
Because I couldn't believe it!

19:35.210 --> 19:40.470
I still hope it's just some misunderstanding!

19:41.940 --> 19:44.430
But because of that...

19:45.720 --> 19:49.650
Since you... didn't kill me back then...

19:49.900 --> 19:54.150
That's why this is happening right now.

20:02.100 --> 20:05.140
Yeah, I'm pretty sure you're right.

20:06.180 --> 20:10.280
I never expected you to corner me like this.

20:13.040 --> 20:18.340
Why didn't I kill you then? I wonder.

20:19.090 --> 20:20.770
Hey, Annie!

20:20.770 --> 20:23.760
There's still a chance that you've
just got a sick sense of humor,

20:23.760 --> 20:28.170
and you're just going along with whatever
Armin says because you're an idiot.

20:28.170 --> 20:30.060
So get down here now!

20:31.060 --> 20:34.180
If you come underground,
that alone proves something!

20:34.180 --> 20:35.980
Come on and prove it!

20:36.900 --> 20:38.690
I can't go down there...

20:38.690 --> 20:41.740
I've failed to become a soldier.

20:41.740 --> 20:44.700
Cut it out already!

20:44.700 --> 20:46.200
Tell us, Annie!

20:46.200 --> 20:48.120
We can still talk...

20:48.120 --> 20:49.530
That's enough.

20:50.150 --> 20:51.920
I can't listen to another word of this.

20:53.220 --> 20:54.510
It's pointless.

20:56.460 --> 20:59.050
I'll tear you apart once again,

20:59.050 --> 21:01.280
female-form Titan!

21:27.540 --> 21:29.130
Armin,

21:29.130 --> 21:32.470
I'm glad I could be a good person for you.

21:33.370 --> 21:35.910
You've won your bet.

21:38.450 --> 21:43.550
But this is where my gamble begins!

21:56.920 --> 21:58.090
Eren!

22:03.920 --> 22:04.740
Mikasa!

22:04.740 --> 22:05.820
We were too late!

22:36.200 --> 22:41.590
If we suppose that I am not me,

22:41.590 --> 22:46.130
Can you say with certainty that you are you?

22:46.780 --> 22:51.660
Will you be able to pick up after yourself

22:51.660 --> 22:56.810
Once your sand-like shell breaks and your heart crumbles?

22:57.090 --> 23:02.020
I could hear someone calling

23:02.310 --> 23:05.920
But now my ears are just ringing

23:06.240 --> 23:11.080
It's as if time has frozen

23:11.380 --> 23:13.990
Now, wake up

23:13.990 --> 23:18.960
I began to walk through a deep dark abyss

23:19.510 --> 23:24.260
As swift as a gale, I escaped for my life

23:24.670 --> 23:28.830
I felt like a living corpse

23:29.240 --> 23:33.960
We break out of our walls

23:34.270 --> 23:40.350
To reunite in worlds we've yet to map

23:53.288 --> 23:57.311
The Female Titan was Annie Leonhart.

23:58.133 --> 24:02.170
Eren is unable to transform in face of the Female Titan.

24:03.111 --> 24:05.215
because he knows it to be Annie.

24:05.215 --> 24:05.911
Mercy: Assault on Stohess, Part 2
because he knows it to be Annie.

24:05.911 --> 24:06.966
Mercy: Assault on Stohess, Part 2
